From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:59:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(guardrails): halt near-duplicate tool-call loops

Local addition (RHOAI3 V21). identical_call_streak_halt keys on
byte-identical arguments, and the read-family/read-cycle guards (0011,
0012) only see recognised read-only pipelines; any other command
(mvn, find | xargs, a script, sed) starts a new phase for them. In the
v21 run (Qwen3.8-27B int4, 2026-09-27/28) five loop shapes each ran
10-40 minutes with no edit and no board call:

- run 44: alternating `mvn dependency:tree | grep "spring"` /
  `... | grep "org.springframework"` (~10 min)
- run 35: `find src/main/java -name "*.java" | xargs grep -l "<package>"`
  with the quoted package growing every call (161+ variants, 23 min)
- run 36: one `grep -o '...{.\{3900,4250\}' brief.json | cut -c 60-120`
  with a varying chained tail, 65+ times (30 min)
- run 37: `cat PetRepository.java | sed -n 'N,N+5p'`, N stepping by one
  and cycling (30 min)
- run 39: `brief.py --section previous_attempts | grep -B20 ...` widened
  to -B50 ... -B1500

Near-duplicate guard: every foreground terminal call and every
idempotent read-tool call is normalised (digit runs -> #, leading
`cd DIR` dropped) with operand identity kept: the quoted literals, query
terms and paths a call names. Two calls (same tool) are near-duplicates
when they are identical after normalisation, or when their shapes
(quoted text as a placeholder) have a difflib token ratio >= 0.75 and
either their operands correspond (equal after digit normalisation, or a
quoted term that grew from / was cut back to the other: run 35, run 44)
or they share the same first chain element and only a chained part
differs (run 36). A different search term or a different file is a
different call. A call makes progress when it names an operand no call
since the last reset named (an empty answer to a new question is
information), or when more than half of its output lines are new since
the last reset.
With hard stops enabled the
turn halts with near_duplicate_loop_halt when 12 of the last 16 observed
calls are non-progressing near-duplicates of the latest one, or when a
cycle of 2-3 calls repeats 6 times position by position; from 8 a loop
warning is appended to the current result. A file edit (write_file,
patch, execute_code, delegate_task, skill_manage), a terminal command
that visibly writes (redirection to a file, rm/mv/cp/tee/..., sed -i,
perl -pi, writing git subcommands, a script body that writes), a
background command or a Kanban board transition resets the history.
Thresholds live in tool_loop_guardrails.near_duplicate. The halt is an
ordinary after_call halt decision, so the runtime records it like the
other guardrails (STOP WORKER_TOOL_LOOP ... guardrail
near_duplicate_loop_halt). No context is mutated: guidance is appended
to the current tool result only.

Upstream 1fec70ea48 (identical_cycle_halt, periods 2-4) only matches
cycles with identical arguments AND results, so it covers none of the
five shapes except a strictly identical alternation; it is not
backported.

Review 2026-09-28 (F2): the first version collapsed every quoted
literal and required new output lines for progress, so 12 distinct
empty package searches and 13 reads of different files sharing
boilerplate halted. Both review probes, 25 distinct empty searches, 25
files with 90% shared lines and sed paging over new content now run
unhalted; the five live shapes and an exact ABAB alternation still
halt. Thresholds are unchanged; run 36 halts up to three calls later
because each distinct chained tail is a new question the first time.

